# Named Exports

Always use named exports. Avoid default exports in TypeScript files.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
export default class AuthController { ... }
export default function login() { ... }
export default { login, register };

// ✅ GOOD
export class AuthController { ... }
export function login() { ... }
export { login, register };
```

Named exports improve discoverability, enable better IDE auto-imports, and prevent accidental renaming at the import site.
